 To create a simple toast notification using React and Context API, follow these steps:

1. Create a new Context for the toast messages.

```jsx
import { createContext } from 'react';

export const ToastContext = createContext();
```

2. Wrap your application with the Provider component of the Context. This will make the context available to all child components.

```jsx
// In your main App component
import { StrictMode, useState } from 'react';
import { ToastContext } from './ToastContext';

function App() {
  // Add state and functions for handling toast messages here
  const [toasts, setToasts] = useState([]);

  function addToast(message) {
    setToasts([...toasts, message]);
    setTimeout(() => setToasts(prevToasts => prevToasts.filter((_, i) => i !== prevToasts.length - 1)), 3000);
  }

  return (
    <StrictMode>
      <ToastContext.Provider value={{ toasts, addToast }}>
        {/* Your app components go below */}
      </ToastContext.Provider>
    </StrictMode>
  );
}
```

3. Create a custom Toast component that consumes the context and displays the toast messages.

```jsx
// In a separate file or in the same file below your App component
import React from 'react';
import { ToastContext } from './ToastContext';

const Toast = () => {
  const { toasts } = React.useContext(ToastContext);

  return (
    <div className="toast-container">
      {toasts.map((msg, index) => (
        <div key={index} className="toast">{msg}</div>
      ))}
    </div>
  );
};

export default Toast;
```

4. Use the `Toast` component in your JSX wherever you want the toast notifications to appear.

```jsx
// In any component or in your main App component
<Toast />
```

Now you have a simple toast notification system using React

